# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.wasm
wasm_exec.js
examples/wasm-components-demo/*.css
examples/wasm-components-demo/screenshot.png
examples/showcase-app/*.css
examples/collab-editor-app/static/*.css

# gio-counter-demo build output (make build-*, see its own Makefile) --
# dist/ holds every -target's packaged output; the .syso is a stray
# Windows icon-resource object gogio -target windows drops in the
# package directory itself, not under -o's own output path.
examples/gio-counter-demo/dist/
examples/gio-counter-demo/*.syso

# make showcase-dist output (docs/deploy.md)
/dist/

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# editors/vscode-xango's own packaged output (make vscode-package,
# root Makefile) -- a build artifact, not source.
*.vsix

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# built example servers
examples/collab-editor-app/server
examples/echo-ssr-demo/echo-ssr-demo
examples/gin-ssr-demo/gin-ssr-demo

# built binaries (go build in the repo root)
/canvas-editor-showcase
/collabhub
/docsh

# built binaries at the repo root
/translateserver
/docstore-bin
local-ci-report.txt

# local stack settings and secrets (docker-compose.yml)
.env.local
secrets/

/.pdfa11y/
